// A field-replacement update may change the field's TYPE (a "strong" update).
// Because the result is a fresh value, no old observer can ever see the new
// type through it, so retyping a field is sound (proposal-value-semantics-mvp
// §3.1). Here `count` goes from an Integer to a String.
def cell = #{ count = 3, label = "start" };

// Replace `count` with a string. The old `cell` is unaffected; the result is a
// new record whose `count` field is now a String.
#{ cell | count = "three" }

// The harness checks:
//@ expect: clean
//@ expect-last-value: #{count = "three", label = "start"}
